items.body:
**Two changes reduce fullscreen wheel-input backlog: skip the per-wheel pre-render, then drain ready wheel events before drawing, with a fairness bound.** On Windows, a local optimized build reduced 401-event burst stopping latency from **734–791 ms to 110–134 ms**, with correct final positions.

### 1. Skip the pre-render for wheel events

**[codex-rs/tui/src/app/owned_transcript.rs:284](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/36650394c5b38c2990ccf2a3457165ca3e9d9726/codex-rs/tui/src/app/owned_transcript.rs#L284)** — the `TuiEvent::Mouse` branch currently renders before every event except `Moved`.

Extend that exclusion to `ScrollUp` and `ScrollDown`. Keep processing each wheel event; let the existing scheduled draw render the accumulated viewport position. Other mouse events retain their pre-render.

```rust
if !matches!(
    mouse.kind,
    MouseEventKind::Moved | MouseEventKind::ScrollUp | MouseEventKind::ScrollDown
) {
    let size = tui.prepare_draw_size()?;
    self.render_owned_transcript(tui, size)?;
}
```

### 2. Drain ready wheel input before drawing

**[codex-rs/tui/src/tui/event_stream.rs:312](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/36650394c5b38c2990ccf2a3457165ca3e9d9726/codex-rs/tui/src/tui/event_stream.rs#L312)** — change `TuiEventStream::poll_next` from unconditional round-robin preference:

- Add `wheel_events_since_draw: usize`, initialized to `0`.
- After a wheel event, prefer ready input. At **64 consecutive wheel events**, prefer a ready draw. If the preferred source is pending, immediately poll the other source.
- Increment the counter for each wheel event; reset it on other events. After `Draw`, set `poll_draw_first = false` so input is preferred next.
- Preserve every event and its order. No debounce timer, dropped ticks, or merging of opposite directions. The bound prevents sustained wheel input from starving ready frames.

The exact locally tested implementation diff is below; the snippets and links target **0.157.1 / `36650394c5b38c2990ccf2a3457165ca3e9d9726`**.

<details>
<summary>Exact implementation diff (two files)</summary>

```diff
diff --git a/codex-rs/tui/src/app/owned_transcript.rs b/codex-rs/tui/src/app/owned_transcript.rs
index 18ba695600..8089ac010d 100644
--- a/codex-rs/tui/src/app/owned_transcript.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/tui/src/app/owned_transcript.rs
@@ -284,7 +284,15 @@ impl App {
         }
         if let TuiEvent::Mouse(mouse) = event {
             let composer_ready = self.chat_widget.prepare_composer_mouse(*mouse);
-            if mouse.kind != crossterm::event::MouseEventKind::Moved {
+            // Wheel bursts only update the viewport position. Drawing before every
+            // tick lets high-rate wheels queue expensive, already obsolete frames.
+            // The scheduled draw below presents the accumulated scroll position.
+            if !matches!(
+                mouse.kind,
+                crossterm::event::MouseEventKind::Moved
+                    | crossterm::event::MouseEventKind::ScrollUp
+                    | crossterm::event::MouseEventKind::ScrollDown
+            ) {
                 let size = tui.prepare_draw_size()?;
                 self.render_owned_transcript(tui, size)?;
             }
diff --git a/codex-rs/tui/src/tui/event_stream.rs b/codex-rs/tui/src/tui/event_stream.rs
index 35afa4bfbb..6c994748ff 100644
--- a/codex-rs/tui/src/tui/event_stream.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/tui/src/tui/event_stream.rs
@@ -166,6 +166,7 @@ pub struct TuiEventStream<S: EventSource + Default + Unpin = CrosstermEventSourc
     resume_stream: WatchStream<()>,
     terminal_focused: Arc<AtomicBool>,
     poll_draw_first: bool,
+    wheel_events_since_draw: usize,
     #[cfg(unix)]
     suspend_context: crate::tui::job_control::SuspendContext,
     #[cfg(unix)]
@@ -187,6 +188,7 @@ impl<S: EventSource + Default + Unpin> TuiEventStream<S> {
             resume_stream,
             terminal_focused,
             poll_draw_first: false,
+            wheel_events_since_draw: 0,
             #[cfg(unix)]
             suspend_context,
             #[cfg(unix)]
@@ -312,27 +314,44 @@ impl<S: EventSource + Default + Unpin> Stream for TuiEventStream<S> {
     type Item = TuiEvent;
 
     fn poll_next(mut self: Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut Context<'_>) -> Poll<Option<Self::Item>> {
-        // approximate fairness + no starvation via round-robin.
-        let draw_first = self.poll_draw_first;
+        // Drain ready wheel ticks before drawing intermediate scroll positions,
+        // with a bound that keeps continuous input from starving display frames.
+        const MAX_WHEEL_EVENTS_PER_FRAME: usize = 64;
+        let draw_first = if self.wheel_events_since_draw >= MAX_WHEEL_EVENTS_PER_FRAME {
+            true
+        } else if self.wheel_events_since_draw > 0 {
+            false
+        } else {
+            self.poll_draw_first
+        };
         self.poll_draw_first = !self.poll_draw_first;
 
-        if draw_first {
-            if let Poll::Ready(event) = self.poll_draw_event(cx) {
-                return Poll::Ready(event);
-            }
-            if let Poll::Ready(event) = self.poll_crossterm_event(cx) {
-                return Poll::Ready(event);
+        let result = if draw_first {
+            match self.poll_draw_event(cx) {
+                Poll::Pending => self.poll_crossterm_event(cx),
+                ready => ready,
             }
         } else {
-            if let Poll::Ready(event) = self.poll_crossterm_event(cx) {
-                return Poll::Ready(event);
+            match self.poll_crossterm_event(cx) {
+                Poll::Pending => self.poll_draw_event(cx),
+                ready => ready,
             }
-            if let Poll::Ready(event) = self.poll_draw_event(cx) {
-                return Poll::Ready(event);
+        };
+        if let Poll::Ready(Some(event)) = &result {
+            if matches!(event, TuiEvent::Mouse(mouse) if matches!(
+                mouse.kind,
+                crossterm::event::MouseEventKind::ScrollUp
+                    | crossterm::event::MouseEventKind::ScrollDown
+            )) {
+                self.wheel_events_since_draw = self.wheel_events_since_draw.saturating_add(1);
+            } else {
+                self.wheel_events_since_draw = 0;
+                if matches!(event, TuiEvent::Draw) {
+                    self.poll_draw_first = false;
+                }
             }
         }
-
-        Poll::Pending
+        result
     }
 }
```

</details>

### Reproduce / evidence

Windows x64 build 26200; Codex CLI **0.157.1**; tlbx **10.17.0** (browser/xterm.js terminal). Set `[tui] fullscreen_transcript = true`, resume a long conversation, spin a Logitech free-spin wheel over the transcript, then stop or reverse. The stock build visibly starts late and continues scrolling after input stops. Expected: prompt movement and stopping while preserving scroll distance.

Stock npm executable versus local `cargo build --release -p codex-cli`, same release tag and terminal setup; no terminal changes. Offline fixture: 40 responses × 300 numbered lines. Synthetic wheel input travels through xterm mouse reporting. Timing is from the last emitted mouse input to the final visible transcript-buffer change:

| 401-event burst, three runs | Stock | Patched |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Reverse every 10 events | 734 / 753 / 791 ms | 116 / 112 / 114 ms |
| Same direction | 784 / 745 / 756 ms | 110 / 134 / 126 ms |

All final-position checks passed. Paced-input tests also passed. A manual Logitech free-spin test confirmed a substantial improvement after restarting into the patched build.

**Validation limits:** 13 focused tests passed, including ready-input ordering, yielding a frame after 64 ticks, immediate short-tail drawing, and an accumulated-viewport snapshot. An earlier broad TUI run had 78 failures and 5 timeouts; no unchanged baseline was established, so the full suite is not claimed green. Linux/macOS are untested. The timing comparison uses stock release versus a local optimized build, not two identically built binaries.
